# Fraud rule engine, every endpoint.
#
# Runs in Visual Studio, Rider, and the VS Code REST Client extension. Send a request with the
# link or gutter arrow the editor puts above it.
#
# The stack must be up: docker compose up -d --build
#
# Event identifiers here are fixed rather than generated, so the collection can be run more than
# once and the records stay findable. That also means a second send of the same request returns
# the verdict the first one produced, which is the idempotency behaviour rather than a mistake.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@apiKey = dev-local-key-0123456789
@customerId = CUST-4471

### Liveness. No key: an orchestrator does not have one.
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness. Reports the database, so this is the one that turns 503 when it is unreachable.
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### Which rules are live, on what thresholds, and the weights behind a score.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/rules
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Approve. An ordinary purchase, in the afternoon, nothing to say about it.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "req-approve-0001",
  "transactionId": "TXN-000101",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "accountId": "ACC-9920",
  "amount": 240.00,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "category": "Groceries",
  "channel": "ChipAndPin",
  "merchantId": "MERCH-1180",
  "merchantName": "Checkers Sandton",
  "countryCode": "ZA",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-01T14:30:00+02:00"
}

### Review. A large cash withdrawal at 02:14, which is a high value hit plus an unusual hour.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "req-review-0001",
  "transactionId": "TXN-000123",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "accountId": "ACC-9920",
  "amount": 48500.00,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "category": "CashWithdrawal",
  "channel": "Atm",
  "merchantId": "MERCH-771",
  "merchantName": "ATM Sandton City",
  "countryCode": "ZA",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-02T02:14:00+02:00"
}

### Review on one rule. A deny listed merchant reaches review by itself but cannot decline alone.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "req-review-0002",
  "transactionId": "TXN-000124",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "accountId": "ACC-9920",
  "amount": 300.00,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "category": "Groceries",
  "channel": "Ecommerce",
  "merchantId": "MERCH-DENY-0001",
  "merchantName": "Blocked Merchant",
  "countryCode": "ZA",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-03T11:05:00+02:00"
}

### Decline. Two corroborating signals: a deny listed merchant and a high value amount.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "req-decline-0001",
  "transactionId": "TXN-000125",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "accountId": "ACC-9920",
  "amount": 60000.00,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "category": "Retail",
  "channel": "Ecommerce",
  "merchantId": "MERCH-DENY-0003",
  "merchantName": "Blocked Merchant",
  "countryCode": "ZA",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-04T13:40:00+02:00"
}

### Repeat delivery. Same event as the decline above with the amount changed, which a queue will
# eventually do. Returns the original assessment, same identifier and same time, not a new one.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "eventId": "req-decline-0001",
  "transactionId": "TXN-000125",
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "accountId": "ACC-9920",
  "amount": 25.00,
  "currency": "ZAR",
  "category": "Retail",
  "channel": "Ecommerce",
  "merchantId": "MERCH-DENY-0003",
  "merchantName": "Blocked Merchant",
  "countryCode": "ZA",
  "occurredAt": "2026-09-04T13:40:00+02:00"
}

### Rejected input. Every problem at once rather than one per round trip.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{}

### A batch where one item is bad. The bad one is refused by position and the rest are kept.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/batch
Content-Type: application/json
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "transactions": [
    {
      "eventId": "req-batch-0001",
